  ## Description
  
  Detect cloud victim data collection behavior.
  
  ## Composition
  
  **Sequence**: Signals must be tracked across time, and correlated based on a succession of events. Particularly useful for weak signals, but which assembled over time with reinforcing signal provide a high fidelity detection - for example, anomalous logons.
  
  Correlate cloud identity telemetry with control plane actions.
  
  ## Threats addressed
  
  | Threat vector | Criticality | Kill chain |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | [Azure Gather Victim Data](../threats/azure-gather-victim-data.md) | High | Reconnaissance |
  
  ## Signals
  
  ### Unusual cloud directory enumeration
  
  Enumerations from anomalous identities and hosts.
  
  | Property | Value |
  | --- | --- |
  | Severity | Medium |
  | Methodology | Behavioural |
  | Effort | 3 |
  | Entities | Account, Hostname |
  | Data availability | Complete |
  | Data requirements | Cloud activity and identity logs |
  | Log sources | `Azure AD AuditLogs`, `Entra ID SignInLogs` |
  | Implemented by | [Shai-Hulud Sentinel Rule](../rules/shai-hulud-sentinel-rule.md) |
  | UUID | `00000000-0000-4000-8199-000000000001` |
  
  **Existing detectors**
  
  | Detector | Technology | Description | Link |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | Sentinel cloud enumeration baseline | Microsoft Sentinel | Correlates unusual list operations from cloud identities. | [Reference](https://example.com/detectors/cloud-enumeration) |
  
  **Examples**
  
  1. Baseline KQL sequence for identity enumeration. ([source](https://example.com/examples/cloud-enumeration))
  
  ```sql
  AuditLogs
  | where OperationName has "List"
  | where Result =~ "success"
  | take 1
  ```
  
  ## Signal rule coverage
  
  | Signal | Rules | Platforms and status |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | Unusual cloud directory enumeration | [Shai-Hulud Sentinel Rule](../rules/shai-hulud-sentinel-rule.md) | Microsoft Sentinel `STAGING` |
  
